    "created_at": "2023-11-13T07:57:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-11-13T08:25:37Z",
    "body": "No I am talking about background videos of a video file type, not gif file type loaded with the background-image property.\r\n\r\nWhile I guess technically it does belong under CSS, the specification would best be developed in synchronization with the current HTML issues, since, from a site visitor's perspective, I don't care whether the video was added via HTML, CSS, or JavaScript for that matter; I don't want any video to auto-play.\r\n\r\nHowever, it appears I was mistaken. Various examples I am finding via search use the video tag, which is covered by the current issue, and there is no mention in the CSS spec for background-image of supporting video.\r\n\r\nMy apologies for the distraction.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
