    "created_at": "2025-08-29T12:11:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-29T12:11:44Z",
    "body": "Users should be able to choose to play any particular video, even if they have `prefers-reduced-motion` enabled. Because videos authored to be autoplaying often lack authored play/pause controls, should a video that's prevented from autoplaying automatically have controls displayed, as if the video had the `controls` attribute?\n\nDo all user agents provide means to play/pause <video> in addition to `controls`? I know at least some have them as an option in a context menu but I don't know if that's universal (I'm especially wondering about mobile browsers).\n\nEven if videos already have other ways to play/pause, displaying the native video controls would be a reliable signal that the content is a video and not a static image.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
